[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-98d4d493-6e4e-48a5-80d5-5d3d0061ba6d\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Papers</p></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"98d4d493-6e4e-48a5-80d5-5d3d0061ba6d\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>Prism: A Multi-solution Reasoning and Synthesis Framework for Repository-Level Issue Resolution</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>Large language model (LLM)-based agents have achieved notable success in repository-level issue resolution, yet existing frameworks still face two key bottlenecks: insufficient diversity among candidate repair solutions and limited ability to combine complementary strengths across candidate solutions.<br>\nTo address these challenges, we introduce \\textsc{Prism}, a multi-solution reasoning and synthesis framework that adopts a coarse-to-fine paradigm to systematically generate, refine, and integrate diverse repair solutions. \\textsc{Prism} comprises three stages: (1) a \\emph{global exploration} mechanism with contrastive semantic constraints that broadens the search space by encouraging divergence across historical solutions; (2) an \\emph{A* algorithm}-inspired \\emph{local exploration} mechanism that identifies suitable branching points to generate divergent sub-solutions; and (3) a multi-agent collaborative \\emph{solution synthesis} process where reviewer and judge agents jointly evaluate, complement, and integrate partially correct candidate solutions. We evaluate \\textsc{Prism} on \\textit{SWE-bench Verified} and \\textit{SWE-bench-Live Lite}. With \\textit{Claude-4.6-Sonnet} and \\textit{DeepSeek-V3.2-Reasoner}, \\textsc{Prism} achieves \\emph{Pass@1} rates of 82.0% and 80.0% on \\textit{SWE-bench Verified}, respectively, outperforming the compared baselines. On \\textit{SWE-bench-Live Lite}, designed to reduce data leakage concerns, \\textsc{Prism} outperforms the reported baselines. Further analyses show that \\textsc{Prism} expands the solution space and that its solution synthesis stage uniquely resolves 15 issues unaddressed by isolated candidates.</p>\n<p></p><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1145/3832783.3837451\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> DOI</a><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/yibowang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Yibo Wang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Northeastern University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/guotianwang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Guotian Wang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Northeastern University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/zhihaopeng\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Zhihao Peng<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Northeastern University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/yingwang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Ying Wang\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/yingwang/3b62f02a-ea4a-4c73-b40a-e97d0b838286/micro-avatar?1793538910000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Ying Wang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Northeastern University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/changxu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Chang Xu\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/changxu/282612ab-429c-471a-bed1-c127c66f0c39/micro-avatar?1793538909000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Chang Xu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Nanjing University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/zhiliangzhu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Zhiliang Zhu\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/zhiliangzhu/bde7f9df-ec52-4a18-8376-0dbbed1d5a7e/micro-avatar?1785334227000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Zhiliang Zhu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Northeastern University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/155/Prism-A-Multi-solution-Reasoning-and-Synthesis-Framework-for-Repository-Level-Issue-\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-98d4d493-6e4e-48a5-80d5-5d3d0061ba6d').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
